(global_label "ADXL_INT1" (shape passive) (at 58.42 130.81 270) (effects (font (size 1.0 1.0)) (justify left)) (uuid 8e683b74-492d-5ad2-9922-f8ac2e99f09c))
(text "the BMP581 datasheet gives no external-component BOM and asks for no supply capacitor, so 100 nF each is the\nminimum HF bypass rather than a datasheet value, and the 1 uF C55/C57 that used to sit beside them are gone.\nU23 ADXL375: CS = ADXL_CS, SDA/SDI = ADXL_MOSI, SDO = ADXL_MISO, SCL/SCLK = ADXL_SCK, INT1 = ADXL_INT1.\nPer the pin function table, pin 3 (RESERVED) goes to VS and pin 11 (RESERVED) to GND; pin 10 (NC) is left open.\nINT2 = ADXL_INT2 on dedicated GPIO21. VS and VDD I/O are both on V3V3_ANA.\nDECOUPLING IS THE DATASHEET'S OWN AND IS THE OTHER WAY ROUND FROM THE OTHER TWO SENSOR PAGES. \"Power Supply\nDecoupling\": \"A 1 uF tantalum capacitor (CS) at VS and a 0.1 uF ceramic capacitor (CI/O) at VDD I/O placed close\nto the ADXL375 supply pins are recommended\". So C59 is 1 uF on VS and C60 is 100 nF on VDD I/O - one cap per\npin, the big one on the ANALOG supply - and the C58 100 nF / C61 1 uF that mirrored the other pages are removed.\nA ceramic stands in for the datasheet's tantalum (lower ESR, and no tantalum is wanted on a 3.3 V sensor rail).\nThe datasheet's optional extras - a <=100 R resistor or ferrite in series with VS, or 10 uF on VS - are NOT\nfitted: VS is an LDO output here, not a switcher rail." (at 10 150 0) (effects (font (size 1.1 1.1)) (justify left top)) (uuid f4ea28a5-e479-5ce6-947d-44306223dcac))
